---
layout: layouts/base.liquid
---
{% comment %}
You may have noticed that both this file and `strip.liquid` both use
`base.liquid` as a layout, despite being layouts themselves. There's nothing
actually wrong with that; I'm just pointing it out to say it's intentional!
(https://www.11ty.dev/docs/layout-chaining/)

Pages with a `section` in their front matter (About, Support, Links) show the
text written for them in the Studio, falling back to the page's own file.
{% endcomment %}<div class="subPage paperDiv">
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  {%- if section %}
  {{ sections[section] | markdown }}
  {%- else %}
  {{ content }}
  {%- endif %}
</div>
